    /// What a project's month of charging cost the site
    ///
    /// Each location is cut in its **own** time zone (its own, else the project's,
    /// else UTC, and each entry says which), so the project month is the union of
    /// its locations' months: the ended sessions that started in `month` at each,
    /// whole, under that location's supply contract, exactly as
    /// `/locations/{id}/energy-cost` answers it. `month` is required, because a
    /// project's locations may be in different zones and it has no single "now".
    ///
    /// `locations` has one entry per location with a session (ended or running)
    /// that started in the month. `totals` is the exact sum of the `computed`
    /// locations' amounts **per currency**, never across currencies and never over
    /// a location that has no amount; `locationsWithoutCost` counts the locations
    /// that have none, those with nothing to price (`noSessions`) not counted.
    /// Sessions at a charger that sits at no location have no supply contract to be
    /// priced under: they are counted in `sessionsWithoutLocation` and are in no
    /// location and no total. Test sessions are excluded and counted.
    ///
    /// Priced when asked, at the contracts in force now (`priceBasis:
    /// currentContract`), and in the mode of the credential (an assistant's is
    /// always live). A month with more sessions than one read lists is refused,
    /// never totalled over a subset.
